text:
lina: Quick Q — I'm planning to bump replicas for inference-api from 3 -> 5 to smooth traffic during the weekend cutover. Thinking to tweak the Deployment rollingUpdate to maxSurge: 30%, maxUnavailable: 0, add a 60s preStop, and update the Terraform PDB (minAvailable: 1). Also need to rotate the TLS secret at the same time. Any obvious gotchas?

matt: A couple notes: maxUnavailable: 0 is quite aggressive. For Deployments I usually do maxUnavailable: 1 and maxSurge: 25% to avoid overcommitting node resources. If nodes are tight you can hit OOMs during the surge. PDB minAvailable: 1 is fine for a 5-replica app.

matt: Add a readinessProbe delay so new pods aren't marked ready until KV cache warms — avoids traffic thrash. Secret rotation won't automatically restart pods unless you trigger it (K8s doesn't watch Secret contents). Two quick options: annotate the pod template with a secret hash in CI or run `kubectl rollout restart deploy/inference-api -n prod`.

lina: can you paste a tiny TF snippet for the rolling update + advice for annotation?

matt: sure:

```hcl
resource "kubernetes_deployment" "inference_api" {
  metadata {
    name = "inference-api"
    namespace = "prod"
  }
  spec {
    replicas = 5
    strategy {
      type = "RollingUpdate"
      rolling_update {
        max_surge = "25%"
        max_unavailable = 1
      }
    }
    template {
      metadata {
        annotations = {
          # CI should stamp: secret-revision = "v1234"
        }
      }
      # ... rest omitted
    }
  }
}
```

matt: To force a rollout from CI after secret rotation you can patch the deployment metadata: 
`kubectl patch deploy inference-api -n prod -p '{"spec":{"template":{"metadata":{"annotations":{"secret-revision":"$REV"}}}}}'` 
or just `kubectl rollout restart deploy/inference-api -n prod` if you prefer manual step.

kevin: Also check HPA targets and cluster autoscaler behavior. If CA is scaling down while you're surging, pods can get evicted. Consider temporarily raising desired node pool size or set a short maintenance window so CA doesn't autoscale down mid-rollout.

kevin: For graceful evictions use the preStop + `terminationGracePeriodSeconds: 90` and ensure the drain task uses `--grace-period=90 --ignore-daemonsets` so connections drain.

olivia: Oncall heads-up: I can monitor the canary rollout 10:30–11:00 PT. Please post canary % + Prometheus queries or an alert dashboard in #eng-oncall when you start.

deploy-bot: Deploy scheduled by lina at 2024-06-10T17:45:00Z — initial canary 10% (auto-scaling enabled).

lina: thanks! I'll open the TF PR with max_surge=25% / max_unavailable=1, add the readinessProbe change, and put CI step to stamp `secret-revision`. I'll ping @olivia before kicking the canary :thumbsup:

matt: SGTM. If you want extra safety we can run a manual 1-pod canary first (scale to 6, then cut traffic).

lina: let's do manual 1-pod canary then automated 10% after green checks. I'll post runbook steps in the PR description.
